.*
.* WRKLIB: the libraries a name selects, with their options. The first
.* entry is blank: option 1 there creates a library.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIBATR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ASPDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIBTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=LIBS VARS='OPT LIB LIBATR ASPDEV LIBTEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/WLKEYS' NAME=WLKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKLIB KEYL=WLKEYS HELP=WRKLIB ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Libraries
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LIBS VIEWS=2 EXTACT=YES.(No libraries selected)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 1'.1=Create
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGLIB LIB(&LIB.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CPYLIB FROMLIB(&LIB.)'.3=Copy
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?DLTLIB LIB(&LIB.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPLIB LIB(&LIB.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPLIB LIB(&LIB.) OUTPUT(*PRINT)'.6=Print
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPOBJD OBJ(QSYS/&LIB.) OBJTYPE(*LIB)'.8=Display library description
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?SAVLIB LIB(&LIB.)'.9=Save
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=10 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?RSTLIB SAVLIB(&LIB.)'.10=Restore
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=11 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?SAVCHGOBJ LIB(&LIB.)'.11=Save changed objects
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=12 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD WRKOBJ OBJ(&LIB./*ALL)'.12=Work with objects
:LISTACT HELP='WRKLIB/OPTIONS' OPTION=14 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CLRLIB LIB(&LIB.)'.14=Clear
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKLIB/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIBATR' VAR=LIBATR USAGE=OUTPUT.Attribute
:LISTGRP COL=ASPGRP.ASP
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ASPDEV' VAR=ASPDEV USAGE=OUTPUT.Device
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIBTEXT' VAR=LIBTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT LIB LIBATR ASPGRP LIBTEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT LIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11 and 12 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKLIB.Work with Libraries - Help
:P.The libraries the name selects. Type an option next to a library;
option 1 on the blank first line, with a name typed on the command
line, creates one. F17 positions the list at the name on the command
line; F11 shows the names alone.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display names only
:PD.Shows the list with the names alone, so more fit on a page.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIB/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBATR'.Attribute
:P.The attribute of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPDEV'.ASP device
:P.The ASP device of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIB/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Library (CHGLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Copy
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to copy it. The Copy Library
(CPYLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Library (DLTLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Library (DSPLIB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Print
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print it. The Display
Library (DSPLIB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Display library description
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to display library
description it. The Display Object Description (DSPOBJD) command runs
for the entry.
:PT.9=Save
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to save it. The Save Library
(SAVLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.10=Restore
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to restore it. The Restore
Library (RSTLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.11=Save changed objects
:PD.Type 11 next to an entry and press Enter to save changed objects it.
The Save Changed Objects (SAVCHGOBJ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with objects
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with objects it.
The Work with Objects (WRKOBJ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.14=Clear
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to clear it. The Clear
Library (CLRLIB) command is prompted for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
